body:
Part of #323 / #305. Owns the bounded run-directory pagination finding from [CodeRabbit review of #331](https://github.com/open-hax/knoxx/pull/331#pullrequestreview-5260130163).

Current #331 adds the provider/query ports but has no production caller of `run-queries/list!`; only its tests use it. The models route first adopts this port in #339. This follow-up is a required predecessor of #339, within the all-merged objective.

Deliver an independently reviewable PR that pages Mongo run snapshots in deterministic newest-first order and bounds decoded results by page size. Preserve expiry and exact tenant/principal authorization. Fetch further pages until the requested visible count is reached or the source is exhausted; never limit before filtering in a way that skips visible authorized results. Keep immutable run/event history intact.

Qualification must include:
- real native Mongo proof with retained expired rows, interleaved foreign principals, equal timestamps, cursor continuation and a limit smaller than the unauthorized leading page;
- bounded per-page decoding and index/query evidence rather than merely a top-level `take`;
- explicit compatibility for existing canonical EDN snapshots that lack any newly introduced sortable metadata, plus legacy documents; no silent omissions or invented chronology;
- equivalent Clio query behavior and fresh authorization, preserving return order/vector shape;
- actual models/listing HTTP proof when consumed by #339, full backend/server checks, both current-head reviewers and resolved conversations.

Do not mark this complete on task creation or move the finding out of #331 without reviewer adjudication. No PR exists yet; #331 remains under review and the requested boundary is awaiting CodeRabbit response.
